{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"automate-excel","displayName":"Automate Excel","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/zways/skills/automate-excel","publisherHandle":"zways","publisherDisplayName":"zway","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/zways","version":"0.1.3","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1772774736664,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/automate-excel/card?ownerHandle=zways&version=0.1.3","sha256":"95d817d73aa80c4c6fa6ea80cb231e702d6e087a3d8be2dc94690cb812f93b79","size":2379,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"ffcad8eb2eef875aa576dccf89fcfb5309d2703d6d8e506e31b399875d828a1c","bundleFingerprints":["f047fe720523b58577afb91eda377452915a1ba73238c9324b5a2eae2f7a9374","22a9960ada8ef339c35b863bcedb8526e0b1aa887b83ed7efb5e82dd7ad312ec"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":8629,"sha256":"44090d00159a70aa607bca6bfc8637770f1c11be12fe0ff57a5ef392ce8bc42d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"examples.md","size":5664,"sha256":"b66536d4c2840975963db14f11db927180e77bdbfd1afc3ae84e228fa7011bf2","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"reference.md","size":6110,"sha256":"93f3c679c0f9646f829578904bbd4d2fc9c0f7ac55f3cb61b3918b9bd6732131","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":42,"sha256":"5c51994177be4eca9a434d998c236f52638423cfa1e1861ea1ec62bf828de898","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/_make_test_data.py","size":2083,"sha256":"e29d29bb10276af3ba6ac5a03425347e6b069957996966893dfcad65b9a489b2","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/aggregate_excel.py","size":2802,"sha256":"ec73efec6780d7e457fe48d21c40799f0b4287d5eddad105109b83c0e0756a29","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/csv_to_excel.py","size":2415,"sha256":"4bdc1803c0e1d9cd1479acf8e5463a8be857bf1c9115d8f93755be4633be30e3","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/deduplicate_excel.py","size":2079,"sha256":"78e4ac5855f0b1a4f815397bbcc7d914c7c5009008c2f5b2d4095149d476e0de","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/excel_to_csv.py","size":1438,"sha256":"c42a71ba2d2275a2d9b91be7f53a9edca3ad5bb017fa7cfaac9428c02423c349","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/filter_excel.py","size":3213,"sha256":"874987642d02cee809977ecf19fc05e246c0faf4e6f51e123958ed4431d1f833","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/format_columns_as_text.py","size":3123,"sha256":"b7414c8727c5985aa8d27ff6e9052f41020a29125d2f2d45cb09605fdc4fe6eb","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/format_conditional.py","size":5149,"sha256":"2cd0afbcec37e0563d78ff0404e9c520fca58bd7ba7c00bb92b13f7fde6dfe2f","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/merge_sheets.py","size":2837,"sha256":"cfd08ab9f6e71fcf39133da2cf0ee37ac49ed95b707dba8e2982eb2914f4c711","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/merge_tables.py","size":2820,"sha256":"beb194a8fae9c052f41e2ae035d0abfc463725ce586f470559a86e8f9eae06cc","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/rename_sheets.py","size":3035,"sha256":"cbdba5e1d857978a192f40534563d3ae1150b826ea393a71ecf0e75169b4692f","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/requirements.txt","size":42,"sha256":"5c51994177be4eca9a434d998c236f52638423cfa1e1861ea1ec62bf828de898","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/select_columns.py","size":2502,"sha256":"4ac213c99a7300fadf02eb74985b9cbe85d91350476e1daaf758ace87fc30cce","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/split_excel.py","size":2747,"sha256":"fe4bdfd3d44a864959c4c27809002130240ba73294313c24927247188e02fa2b","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/template_fill.py","size":3685,"sha256":"998bf08ab465b1f9eeba19044a00168ec3261df76aa4afaaee14fabd55eb2b73","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/transpose_excel.py","size":1712,"sha256":"88ea1c213a585fa4792e300be57dfb8fbb0234a010c96498d501af4939dcb212","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/validate_excel.py","size":2135,"sha256":"e33d1823093c8792a8162fede5eb651fb97608a85e67c8c226aece5f6200979a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/vlookup_multi.py","size":3327,"sha256":"986ebeeba566f3856f87d4b57b3f32b3f5afafc537099376efd87e1f44c360ad","contentType":"text/plain"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This Excel automation skill is mostly coherent, but it can overwrite workbooks and can carry unsafe formula-like data into generated Excel files.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789107619358,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"CSV Formula Injection in Generated Excel Workbooks"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/csv_to_excel.py"},"region":{"startLine":36,"endLine":60}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"59bb417a81f8704d"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/csv_to_excel.py`, lines 36-44 and 55-60  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Spreadsheet formula injection  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\nif args.input:\n    path = Path(args.input)\n    if not path.exists():\n        print(f\"File does not exist: {path}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, encoding=args.encoding, sep=args.sep)\n    sheet_name = args.sheet_name or path.stem\n    if len(sheet_name) > 31:\n        sheet_name = sheet_name[:31]\n    df.to_excel(out, sheet_name=sheet_name, index=False, engine=\"openpyxl\")\n```\n\n```python\nwith pd.ExcelWriter(out, engine=\"openpyxl\") as writer:\n    for path in paths:\n        df = pd.read_csv(path, encoding=args.encoding, sep=args.sep)\n        name = path.stem\n        if len(name) > 31:\n            name = name[:31]\n        df.to_excel(writer, sheet_name=name, index=False)\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe script imports CSV values and writes them directly into an Excel workbook without distinguishing untrusted text from spreadsheet formulas. Values beginning with formula-significant characters such as `=`, `+`, `-`, or `@` may be interpreted as formulas when the resulting workbook is opened in Excel or another compatible spreadsheet application.\n\nAn attacker who controls any CSV field can therefore place a formula payload in the generated workbook. Depending on the spreadsheet client and its security configuration, such a formula could create deceptive hyperlinks, access external resources, disclose workbook data through supported functions, or abuse legacy formula features.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker creates or modifies a CSV file processed by the Skill.\n2. The attacker inserts a value such as:\n\n   ```text\n   =HYPERLINK(\"https://attacker.example/login\",\"Open report\")\n   ```\n\n3. A user runs `csv_to_excel.py` against the attacker-controlled CSV.\n4. The value is written to the output workbook without neutralization.\n5. The user opens the generated workbook.\n6. The spreadsheet application interprets the value as a formula, presenting attacker-controlled active content or initiating behavior supported by the client.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe vulnerability affects the integrity and safety of generated workbooks. It can facilitate phishing, deceptive links, external-resource requests, or formula-based disclosure of spreadsheet data.\n\nThe code does not itself grant operating-system privileges or automatically execute shell commands. The ultimate scope depends on the formula capabilities and security controls of the spreadsheet application used to open the workbook.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\nTreat imported CSV fields as untrusted text before exporting them to a workbook.\n\n1. Detect strings whose first non-whitespace character is `=`, `+`, `-`, or `@`.\n2. Prefix such strings with an apostrophe or explicitly set the target Excel cell type and number format to text.\n3. Apply the mitigation to column names as well as data values.\n4. Provide an explicit opt-in option for users who intentionally need formulas preserved.\n5. Add regression tests covering all formula prefixes, leading whitespace, tab characters, and multi-file conversion.\n\nFor example:\n\n```python\nFORMULA_PREFIXES = (\"=\", \"+\", \"-\", \"@\")\n\ndef neutralize_formula(value):\n    if isinstance(value, str) and value.lstrip().startswith(FORMULA_PREFIXES):\n        return \"'\" + value\n    return value\n\ndf = df.map(neutralize_formula)\ndf.columns = [neutralize_formula(str(col)) for col in df.columns]\n```\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Formula Injection Through Template Placeholder Substitution"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/template_fill.py"},"region":{"startLine":17,"endLine":75}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"28ec57b5069f1b36"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/template_fill.py`, lines 17-27 and 70-75  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Spreadsheet formula injection through untrusted template data  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\ndef _replace_placeholders(text, row_dict):\n    if text is None or not isinstance(text, str):\n        return text\n    result = text\n    for col, val in row_dict.items():\n        placeholder = \"{{\" + str(col) + \"}}\"\n        if placeholder in result:\n            result = result.replace(\n                placeholder,\n                str(val) if pd.notna(val) else \"\"\n            )\n    result = re.sub(r\"\\{\\{[^}]+\\}\\}\", \"\", result)\n    return result\n```\n\n```python\nfor col_idx in range(1, max_col + 1):\n    src = ws.cell(row=pattern_row_idx, column=col_idx)\n    cell = ws.cell(row=target_row, column=col_idx)\n    cell.value = _replace_placeholders(src.value, row_dict)\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nValues loaded from the data file are substituted directly into template cells. If a template cell consists solely of a placeholder and the corresponding untrusted value begins with `=`, the resulting `cell.value` begins with `=`. Openpyxl can consequently store that cell as a formula rather than literal text.\n\nThe same issue may arise with other formula-significant prefixes depending on how the resulting workbook is interpreted by the spreadsheet application. No trust boundary, formula-preservation policy, or escaping mechanism is implemented.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker controls a row in the CSV or Excel data source used for template filling.\n2. The template contains a cell such as `{{Website}}`.\n3. The attacker supplies a value such as:\n\n   ```text\n   =HYPERLINK(\"https://attacker.example\",\"View details\")\n   ```\n\n4. `template_fill.py` replaces the placeholder with the attacker-controlled value.\n5. The resulting string is assigned directly to `cell.value`.\n6. The user opens the generated workbook and the spreadsheet client treats the cell as active formula content.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nAn attacker can inject formulas into generated reports and templates, compromising workbook integrity and enabling phishing or external-resource interactions. Formula behavior could also disclose data available to the workbook if supported by the spreadsheet client.\n\nNo direct privilege escalation is demonstrated by the audited code. Impact is primarily within the generated workbook and the privileges of the user and spreadsheet client opening it.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Escape untrusted substituted values when they would make the final cell begin with a formula-significant character.\n2. Distinguish trusted template-authored formulas from untrusted data values.\n3. When a cell contains only a placeholder, explicitly store untrusted output as text.\n4. Consider a secure default that rejects formula-like values and an explicit option to permit trusted formula insertion.\n5. Add tests for CSV and Excel data sources, placeholder-only cells, embedded placeholders, leading whitespace, and all relevant formula prefixes.\n\nA safe substitution layer could use logic such as:\n\n```python\nFORMULA_PREFIXES = (\"=\", \"+\", \"-\", \"@\")\n\ndef as_safe_spreadsheet_text(value):\n    text = str(value)\n    if text.lstrip().startswith(FORMULA_PREFIXES):\n        return \"'\" + text\n    return text\n```\n\nThis function should be applied to every untrusted replacement before it is assigned to `cell.value`.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T08","level":"note","message":{"text":"Unbounded and Unhashed Third-Party Dependencies"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"requirements.txt"},"region":{"startLine":1,"endLine":3}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"5989fd1eb82027b0"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `requirements.txt`, lines 1-3; `scripts/requirements.txt`, lines 1-3  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Non-reproducible dependency resolution and supply-chain exposure  \n**Risk Level**: Low\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```text\nopenpyxl>=3.1.0\npandas>=2.0.0\nxlrd>=2.0.0\n```\n\nThe Skill documentation instructs users to install these dependencies with:\n\n```bash\npip install -r scripts/requirements.txt\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe requirements specify only minimum versions and do not establish upper bounds, exact reviewed versions, or package hashes. Every installation can therefore resolve to different future releases.\n\nThe listed dependencies are established packages, and the audit found no malicious package name or unsafe package index. Nevertheless, mutable dependency resolution reduces build reproducibility and exposes users to future compromised, malicious, or incompatible releases that satisfy the minimum-version constraints.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user follows the documented installation command.\n2. Pip resolves the newest releases satisfying the `>=` constraints.\n3. A future upstream release is compromised or introduces unsafe behavior.\n4. That release is installed without a lock file or hash-based integrity check.\n5. Package code executes during import or when the spreadsheet scripts invoke the affected library.\n\nThis path is conditional on an upstream compromise or unsafe future release; no currently malicious dependency was identified during the audit.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nA compromised dependency would execute with the privileges of the user running the Skill and could potentially access files, environment data, and network resources available to that process. The current project does not request elevated privileges, so the exposure is limited to the invoking user's permissions.\n\nThe immediate confirmed impact is non-reproducible installation behavior and reduced dependency integrity assurance.\n]]>","severity":"Low"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Pin dependencies to exact, reviewed versions using `==`.\n2. Generate a lock file with cryptographic hashes, for example with `pip-tools`.\n3. Install with hash verification:\n\n   ```bash\n   pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt\n   ```\n\n4. Keep the root and `scripts/requirements.txt` files synchronized or replace them with one canonical dependency specification.\n5. Use automated dependency scanning and controlled update reviews.\n6. Test every dependency update before changing the lock file.\n7. Consider upper bounds where exact pins cannot be used.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":40,"primaryLanguage":"Python","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789107459.2258842,"endTime":1789107552.3852584}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"automate-excel","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57e7x3tpcn5yw0c330gjb3pns8e7586-Th31aj/clawscan-skillspector-3153941628/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T06:17:38.521366+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":71,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":192,"executable":false,"size_bytes":8629,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples.md","type":"markdown","lines":152,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5664,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"reference.md","type":"markdown","lines":147,"executable":false,"size_bytes":6110,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"requirements.txt","type":"text","lines":3,"executable":false,"size_bytes":42,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/_make_test_data.py","type":"python","lines":56,"executable":true,"size_bytes":2083,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/aggregate_excel.py","type":"python","lines":75,"executable":true,"size_bytes":2802,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/csv_to_excel.py","type":"python","lines":65,"executable":true,"size_bytes":2415,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/deduplicate_excel.py","type":"python","lines":57,"executable":true,"size_bytes":2079,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/excel_to_csv.py","type":"python","lines":42,"executable":true,"size_bytes":1438,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/filter_excel.py","type":"python","lines":99,"executable":true,"size_bytes":3213,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/format_columns_as_text.py","type":"python","lines":86,"executable":true,"size_bytes":3123,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/format_conditional.py","type":"python","lines":123,"executable":true,"size_bytes":5149,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/merge_sheets.py","type":"python","lines":78,"executable":true,"size_bytes":2837,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/merge_tables.py","type":"python","lines":67,"executable":true,"size_bytes":2820,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/rename_sheets.py","type":"python","lines":81,"executable":true,"size_bytes":3035,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/requirements.txt","type":"text","lines":3,"executable":false,"size_bytes":42,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/select_columns.py","type":"python","lines":66,"executable":true,"size_bytes":2502,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/split_excel.py","type":"python","lines":76,"executable":true,"size_bytes":2747,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/template_fill.py","type":"python","lines":92,"executable":true,"size_bytes":3685,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/transpose_excel.py","type":"python","lines":49,"executable":true,"size_bytes":1712,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/validate_excel.py","type":"python","lines":66,"executable":true,"size_bytes":2135,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/vlookup_multi.py","type":"python","lines":79,"executable":true,"size_bytes":3327,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-088a9aca109b48759a090e55cb1fd82d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill description is broad enough to activate on many ordinary spreadsheet-related requests, which can cause the agent to invoke file-processing capabilities in situations where they were not clearly needed. Over-broad activation increases the chance of unnecessary access to local files and unintended data modification workflows, especially because this skill includes read/write and merge operations.","remediation":"Narrow the description to explicit, high-confidence triggers such as requests that directly mention Excel file transformation, workbook merging, CSV/XLSX conversion, or spreadsheet validation. Add non-trigger examples and require confirmation when the request only generally mentions tables, reports, or spreadsheet-like data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-2644ff22a9e340c3a942bf74b044dea8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":8,"end_line":8},"finding":null,"explanation":"The invocation guidance says to apply the skill whenever the user needs Excel processing, batch conversion, or report generation, but it does not define boundaries or prerequisites for safe use. This ambiguity can lead the agent to select the skill without confirming file paths, write targets, or whether the user actually wants filesystem changes, increasing the risk of unintended operations.","remediation":"Add clear trigger constraints: invoke only when the user explicitly asks to operate on spreadsheet files or tabular file conversion, and require confirmation before any write, overwrite, merge, rename, or batch operation. Include explicit exclusions for purely conceptual questions or cases where no file manipulation is requested.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":8,"end_line":8}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e86929112c274bccbbe7c84c7b16b372","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":53,"end_line":53},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill provides write and append examples, including saving back to an existing workbook, without an upfront warning about destructive changes or overwrite risk. In an agent context, this omission is dangerous because it normalizes in-place modification and may cause loss of original data, corruption of reports, or accidental alteration of sensitive spreadsheets.","remediation":"Add an explicit safety warning before all write operations stating that scripts may create, overwrite, or modify files. Default to writing to a new output path, recommend backups, and require explicit user confirmation before saving over an existing file or performing batch writes.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":53,"end_line":53}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-e5c1777ca6794266931b918e886ae66d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"examples.md","start_line":1,"end_line":152},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file’s instructional content, headings, and example descriptions are entirely in Chinese, which effectively forces a specific language for users. The policy allows locale or language constraints only when the skill offers user choice or clearly documents and justifies the restriction.","remediation":"Provide a language option or bilingual documentation, or explicitly document that the skill is intended for Chinese-speaking users and why that locale restriction is necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples.md","start_line":1,"end_line":152}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4d94a32150f74c1baa87c80f8caecc45","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"reference.md","start_line":119,"end_line":145},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents `rename_sheets.py`, `format_conditional.py`, and `format_columns_as_text.py` as having optional `--output` parameters with default overwrite behavior, but it does not warn users that omitting `--output` will modify the original workbook in place. Because this behavior can affect user data integrity, the skill description should explicitly disclose it.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near each default-overwrite option stating that omitting `--output` will modify the source `.xlsx` file in place and may be irreversible. Recommend backing up the file or requiring an explicit flag for in-place edits.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"reference.md","start_line":119,"end_line":145}]},{"id":"AST3","finding_id":"finding-5266be645fb648b78b3b3a8e84c88b8d","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"Dynamic import via __import__()","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"scripts/_make_test_data.py","start_line":50,"end_line":50},"finding":"wb_tpl = __import__(\"openpyxl\").Workbook()","explanation":"Dynamic __import__() can load arbitrary modules at runtime, bypassing static analysis and potentially importing malicious code.","remediation":"Use standard import statements instead of __import__(). If dynamic loading is needed, use importlib with an allowlist of permitted modules.","code_snippet":"df_main.to_csv(\"sample.csv\", index=False, encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\n\n# 模板：第一行表头，第二行占位符 {{姓名}} {{金额}}\nwb_tpl = __import__(\"openpyxl\").Workbook()\nws = wb_tpl.active\nws[\"A1\"], ws[\"B1\"], ws[\"C1\"] = \"姓名\", \"金额\", \"地区\"\nws[\"A2\"], ws[\"B2\"], ws[\"C2\"] = \"{{姓名}}\", \"{{金额}}\", \"{{地区}}\"","intent":null,"tags":["Dangerous Code Execution","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"0b2a7815804cb7a01f6cd6b3314d41b59a72d0ba8d1c59b5c4989a6fc3b3a188","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/_make_test_data.py","start_line":50,"end_line":50}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-d41de0263ae641ecbd8021f331fbbf5a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"scripts/csv_to_excel.py","start_line":2,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"The module docstring is entirely in Chinese, and the CLI description/help text is likewise Chinese-only, which imposes a specific language on users. The policy allows locale constraints only when they are optional or clearly justified, neither of which is present here.","remediation":"Provide bilingual or configurable help/output text, or explicitly document that this skill is intended only for a Chinese-language environment and why that restriction is necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/csv_to_excel.py","start_line":2,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-1edde8f0f7654a3cabb574dae1fdd663","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"scripts/filter_excel.py","start_line":2,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code file contains natural-language usage instructions exclusively in Chinese, and later error/output strings are also Chinese-only. The policy prohibits forcing a specific language or locale unless the skill offers a language choice or clearly documents a justified regional constraint, which is not present here.","remediation":"Provide bilingual or locale-selectable messages and documentation, or explicitly document that the skill is intended only for a Chinese-language environment with justification.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/filter_excel.py","start_line":2,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-0fce83833142420b9a2a26ceb9b5ac98","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"scripts/format_columns_as_text.py","start_line":3,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"The module docstring and command help examples are written entirely in Chinese, and the user-facing argparse descriptions and runtime messages are also Chinese-only. This imposes a specific language on users without opt-in or an explanation that the skill is intentionally region-specific, which matches the locale-policy violation criteria.","remediation":"Provide bilingual user-facing text, add an explicit language selection option, or clearly document that the skill is intended only for a Chinese-speaking context and why that constraint is necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/format_columns_as_text.py","start_line":3,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-fadc9228772e4a40949744e20c0a5835","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"scripts/format_conditional.py","start_line":2,"end_line":65},"finding":null,"explanation":"The module docstring, CLI argument help text, and runtime messages are all written in Chinese, which imposes a specific language on users. The file does not offer localization, a language switch, or any indication that the skill is intentionally limited to a Chinese-speaking context.","remediation":"Add multilingual support or an explicit language-selection option, or document clearly that this skill is intended for a Chinese-only environment with justification. At minimum, provide English alternatives in the help text and user-facing messages.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/format_conditional.py","start_line":2,"end_line":65}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-345cfbc2bd8e49a9986e6264d9663b43","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/merge_sheets.py","start_line":3,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"The module docstring is entirely in Chinese, and the command description is presented only in that language. This creates a language policy concern because the skill imposes a specific locale on users without any opt-in, alternative language support, or stated region-specific justification.","remediation":"Provide bilingual or locale-selectable documentation and messages, or explicitly document that the skill is intended only for a Chinese-speaking or region-specific context. If a locale restriction is necessary, state the justification clearly in the skill description.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/merge_sheets.py","start_line":3,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-187b89051ed441b8ae6e05d6c2602916","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"scripts/merge_sheets.py","start_line":21,"end_line":74},"finding":null,"explanation":"Multiple stderr/stdout messages such as skipped-path notices, failure messages, and the final success message are emitted only in Chinese. Forcing a single language in user-facing strings without opt-in or documented justification violates the natural-language policy criteria.","remediation":"Externalize user-facing strings and support localization or a user-selectable language. At minimum, add an option or environment-based locale choice, or document a justified Chinese-only scope for the tool.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/merge_sheets.py","start_line":21,"end_line":74}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-f4f307cb3a38420eac7a70706e67fc24","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"scripts/merge_tables.py","start_line":3,"end_line":24},"finding":null,"explanation":"The docstring and command-line help text are entirely in Chinese, which imposes a specific language/locale on users of the skill. The file does not offer an alternative language choice or explain that the skill is intentionally limited to a Chinese-speaking context.","remediation":"Document the locale restriction explicitly if this is a region-specific skill, or add bilingual/help text and an opt-in mechanism so users are not forced into a single language unexpectedly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/merge_tables.py","start_line":3,"end_line":24}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-bab6920e346142d2845e3eed67b667cc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/rename_sheets.py","start_line":3,"end_line":17},"finding":null,"explanation":"The docstring and CLI help text are written entirely in Chinese, including the script description and usage guidance. Under the policy rule, forcing a specific language without user opt-in or a documented justification is a natural-language policy violation.","remediation":"Provide bilingual or locale-selectable user-facing text, or document that the skill is intentionally region-specific and why that constraint is required.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/rename_sheets.py","start_line":3,"end_line":17}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-5a1bad759aaa4a87ac4c2deae2babf18","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/select_columns.py","start_line":3,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"The module docstring and CLI help text are entirely in Chinese, which imposes a specific language on all users. Under the policy, locale/language restrictions should either be optional or clearly justified as region-specific; neither is present here.","remediation":"Provide bilingual help text or add an explicit language/locale option. If the skill is intentionally Chinese-only, document that scope and justification clearly in the file or accompanying skill documentation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/select_columns.py","start_line":3,"end_line":22}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-a694a815c7654e7bbe76c9447872d77b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/template_fill.py","start_line":2,"end_line":38},"finding":null,"explanation":"The module docstring, CLI argument descriptions, and runtime status messages are all written only in Chinese. This imposes a specific language on users without any documented opt-in or alternative, which matches the locale/language policy violation criteria.","remediation":"Provide multilingual output or a user-selectable language option, and document the default language behavior. At minimum, add an English alternative or a CLI flag/environment setting to choose the interface language.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/template_fill.py","start_line":2,"end_line":38}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-87151bbf715f46a79d75669088c1e967","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/validate_excel.py","start_line":3,"end_line":20},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file's docstring, argument descriptions, and user-facing output are written only in Chinese, which imposes a specific language on users. The policy allows locale constraints only when users are given a choice or the restriction is clearly documented and justified, neither of which appears here.","remediation":"Provide multilingual or configurable user-facing text, or explicitly document that this skill is intended only for a Chinese-language environment and why that restriction is necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/validate_excel.py","start_line":3,"end_line":20}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-32e37918dc4040e69ee99ac7a921ebe1","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":6,"end_line":8},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill heading and usage guidance are presented in Chinese, while there is no indication that the user can opt into another language. This can violate language/locale policy when a skill imposes a specific language without explicit user choice or documented regional justification.","remediation":"State that the skill can respond in the user's preferred language, or document that Chinese is optional/default only when the user requests it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":6,"end_line":8}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-18a9d03b90e0461882aa08234be98dc2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"examples.md","start_line":5,"end_line":15},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes example commands and code that create or save output files such as `data/merged.xlsx`, but it does not warn users that running these examples will write new files and may overwrite existing outputs. Under the markdown-specific missing-warning criterion, behaviors affecting user data or files should be disclosed.","remediation":"Add a brief warning near the examples stating that the commands write output files, may overwrite existing files if the same path is reused, and should be run on copies or with carefully chosen output paths.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples.md","start_line":5,"end_line":15}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-53dfeed296204fe5970c0daeb776cfce","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":"openpyxl>=3.1.0","explanation":"The dependency is specified with only a lower bound, so builds may resolve to different versions over time. This weakens supply-chain reproducibility and can unexpectedly introduce vulnerable or breaking releases into an automation skill that processes untrusted spreadsheet files.","remediation":"Pin openpyxl to an exact vetted version (or use a lockfile with hashes), review updates through a controlled dependency management process, and regularly scan the pinned version for known advisories.","code_snippet":"openpyxl>=3.1.0\npandas>=2.0.0\nxlrd>=2.0.0","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6cb8bacfc7ca46dbc99203420636c9c14b296925c7bb9388db5b5acb9c8e5bbe","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-749f303cdec84b8db0cb3184d60e4fdf","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: openpyxl has 2 known advisory(ies) (CVE-2017-5992 (Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference in Openpyxl); CVE-2017-5992 (Openpyxl 2.4.1 resolves external entities by default, which allows remote attack)), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":"openpyxl","explanation":"The manifest does not pin openpyxl, and openpyxl has historical advisories related to XML external entity handling. Because this skill parses spreadsheet content, an affected resolved version could expose the environment to malicious workbook input, making the lack of version certainty a real security concern.","remediation":"Pin openpyxl to a version confirmed not affected by the cited advisories, preferably via a lockfile with hashes. Validate that XML-related protections are enabled by default and add dependency scanning in CI.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e842efb2ff752a26115547d1b71a69edcce21a6f8c85c112610d04fa30869871","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-2f9aa5a208494cfc8d04904f5c3c4dbc","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":2,"end_line":null},"finding":"pandas>=2.0.0","explanation":"Using an unpinned pandas version allows dependency drift, making installs non-reproducible and increasing the chance that a newly released vulnerable or incompatible version is pulled in. In a file-processing skill, this can affect integrity and security of data-handling behavior.","remediation":"Pin pandas to an exact tested version or maintain a lockfile with hashes. Update intentionally on a schedule after security review and compatibility testing.","code_snippet":"openpyxl>=3.1.0\npandas>=2.0.0\nxlrd>=2.0.0","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"0604f78352d59a6ec2bc067dd7394f06348c423ba91de199de039e219b650374","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":2,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-bcf86741206748a882936672b84bb11d","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: pandas has 1 known advisory(ies) (CVE-2020-13091 (** DISPUTED ** pandas through 1.0.3 can unserialize and execute commands from an)), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.4,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":2,"end_line":null},"finding":"pandas","explanation":"Dependency has known vulnerabilities (CVEs). Using packages with unpatched security flaws exposes the environment to known exploits.","remediation":"Update the dependency to a patched version that addresses the known CVE. Check OSV (osv.dev) or NVD for details on the vulnerability.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"9604ce04fc16a397c3c073b9e2bc539026bea65f4eab238f6f586124f40d1ff7","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":2,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-988c0a7f714044028201015698bf4d29","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":3,"end_line":null},"finding":"xlrd>=2.0.0\n","explanation":"An unpinned xlrd dependency permits uncontrolled version selection at install time, which is a supply-chain hygiene weakness. Although low severity on its own, it reduces assurance that deployments consistently use a reviewed package version.","remediation":"Pin xlrd to a specific known-good version and use deterministic dependency locking. Add automated dependency scanning and review version changes before release.","code_snippet":"openpyxl>=3.1.0\npandas>=2.0.0\nxlrd>=2.0.0","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"5f69aefe58b0a62240adde4b3802e09244a4dec258facfcc9d9083df8025766c","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":3,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-79848694eddb4aa2bc7d4def2a7fabed","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"scripts/aggregate_excel.py","start_line":3,"end_line":23},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code file contains natural-language strings for the docstring and argument help text exclusively in Chinese. Under the stated policy, forcing a specific language without offering a choice or documenting a justified locale constraint is a natural-language policy violation.","remediation":"Provide bilingual help text or add a language/locale selection mechanism. Alternatively, document that the tool is intentionally region- or language-specific if that constraint is required.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/aggregate_excel.py","start_line":3,"end_line":23}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-c1449e4cccc745489dd832a594d3ee70","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"scripts/excel_to_csv.py","start_line":3,"end_line":20},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code file contains natural-language strings entirely in Chinese in the module docstring and argument/help text. Under the language/locale policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in can be a policy violation when no alternative or justification is provided.","remediation":"Provide bilingual help text or add an option/configuration for the user to choose the interface language. If the tool is intentionally Chinese-only, document the locale constraint and its justification clearly in accompanying documentation or comments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/excel_to_csv.py","start_line":3,"end_line":20}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-573ef2a8e2cd43a892b4ea7b47eddd4a","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/requirements.txt","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":"openpyxl>=3.1.0","explanation":"The dependency specification uses a lower-bound version only, which allows installation of any newer release and makes builds non-reproducible. This increases supply-chain risk because future upstream releases could introduce breaking changes or vulnerable code without review.","remediation":"Pin dependencies to exact versions or tightly bounded ranges, and use a lockfile or constraints file to ensure reproducible installs. Review and update pinned versions through a controlled dependency management process.","code_snippet":"openpyxl>=3.1.0\npandas>=2.0.0\nxlrd>=2.0.0","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6cb8bacfc7ca46dbc99203420636c9c14b296925c7bb9388db5b5acb9c8e5bbe","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/requirements.txt","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-37fba8294b1c4c4d9f88e51b2b2cb81e","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: openpyxl has 2 known advisory(ies) (CVE-2017-5992 (Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference in Openpyxl); CVE-2017-5992 (Openpyxl 2.4.1 resolves external entities by default, which allows remote attack)), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.78,"location":{"file":"scripts/requirements.txt","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":"openpyxl","explanation":"The manifest does not pin openpyxl, so it is impossible to verify from this file alone whether the installed version includes fixes for known advisories. In an Excel-processing skill, this matters more because the package may parse attacker-controlled spreadsheet content, increasing the importance of using a known-safe version.","remediation":"Pin openpyxl to a specific version confirmed not to be affected by known advisories, and document the security-reviewed version in a lockfile. If the skill processes untrusted spreadsheets, ensure secure parser settings are used and keep the package updated to a patched release.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e842efb2ff752a26115547d1b71a69edcce21a6f8c85c112610d04fa30869871","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/requirements.txt","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-037d9a68bda34b1bb2369ad61044a072","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/requirements.txt","start_line":2,"end_line":null},"finding":"pandas>=2.0.0","explanation":"The pandas requirement is unpinned, so deployment may resolve to different versions over time. That weakens reproducibility and can expose the skill to newly introduced vulnerable or incompatible releases from the dependency supply chain.","remediation":"Pin pandas to a vetted exact version and maintain it via a lockfile or constraints file. Add dependency update monitoring so version changes are reviewed before adoption.","code_snippet":"openpyxl>=3.1.0\npandas>=2.0.0\nxlrd>=2.0.0","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"0604f78352d59a6ec2bc067dd7394f06348c423ba91de199de039e219b650374","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/requirements.txt","start_line":2,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-89970b11c10043cc98c7e1d0c133c8f0","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: pandas has 1 known advisory(ies) (CVE-2020-13091 (** DISPUTED ** pandas through 1.0.3 can unserialize and execute commands from an)), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.74,"location":{"file":"scripts/requirements.txt","start_line":2,"end_line":null},"finding":"pandas","explanation":"Because pandas is unpinned, the installed release cannot be verified against known advisories from the manifest alone. This creates uncertainty in a data-processing skill that may ingest untrusted files, where vulnerable deserialization or parsing paths could become relevant depending on runtime usage.","remediation":"